<title>USA: Peoples sees $283,000 SAIF impact.</title>
<headline>Peoples sees $283,000 SAIF impact.</headline>
<dateline>MASSILLON, Ohio 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peoples Financial Corp said on Monday it expected earnings to be reduced by about $283,000 after taxes, due to the impact of recapitalizing its share of the Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
<p>Recent U.S. legislation required all institutions insured by the SAIF to pay a one-time special assessment of $0.657 for every $100 of insured deposits held on March 31, 1995.</p>
